WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
'Good morning Hank. It's Tuesday,' are probably the two consecutive sentences I have spoken most often in my life.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.080
Its either that, or 'I love you. Let's get some pizza.'

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.300
Which you know I said to Mom when I was four,

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.980
and I say to Henry and The Yeti now.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.920
Anyway it's Tuesday,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.000
unless you're me in which case it's actually Saturday morning.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.600
It's Saturday because later this morning The Yeti, Henry, and I are going on vacation,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.160
and on Tuesday I will be on that vacation WITHOUT A  COMPUTER.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.220
That's right, Hank. For the first time since I got this computer it's going to spend a night without me.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.500
To computer: It's okay, shhhhhhhh shh shh Willy(the dog)'s going to stay too. Youll be fine. *mmmwah* You're okay.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.340
Shh its okay, I know, I know.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.340
Well Hank, the reason we are leaving behind computers on this vacation is that

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:41.840
I think sometimes it's good to reset your brain not to expect, like, a new celebrity pregnancy every day.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.280
And more generally, Hank,

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.220
I'm a little worried that I've become addicted to the Internet.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.480
Like a remember talking at the end of 2006 when we were talking about starting Brotherhood 2.0

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.500
Sarah said to me, "I dont understand how you're gonna do this because you already spend so much time on the internet."

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.060
And I was like, "no no no, making videos is going to replace my internet time,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.940
"like the time I now spend falling down the rabbit hole of the internet, I'm going to spend making and editing videos!"

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:09.240
I mean, there wasn't even any Twitter! Or Tumblr! What did I do on the Internet in 2006, Google the weather in Dubai?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:15.720
But, anyway, Hank, in the manner of an addict, I convinced myself that starting an online video project would decrease the amount of time I spent online.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.740
Yeah. *pause*  No.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.740
Now, Hank, I don't want the internet to be confused about my feelings.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.740
I LOVE THE INTERNET.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.820
Like yesterday, Henry and I spent 20 minutes on the Wikipedia article for Whale Sharks

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.940
Because we had a disagreement about whether whale sharks bite humans.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.240
I don't want to brag, but I was right.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.320
And to learn all that stuff about whale sharks cost us nothing.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.560
And I also think that the community and connection I feel because of the internet has made my life richer and better.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.460
However, I am looking forward to doing a lot of reading this week without

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.200
Every 4 minutes a little part of my brain being like, "have you checked your email there might be something important....."

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.920
So, Hank, with that said, I venture into a brave new world where human beings talk to each other in real life and

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.660
Breathe on each other and touch occasionally--it just sounds really germy

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:57.900
But I'm gonna do it because I think it's good for my mental health, particularly in advance of Carnegie *HALLLLLL*

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.480
Which is the sound that my anxiety makes.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:03.960
And speaking of Carnegie Hall, Nerdfighters, if you don't have tickets to Carnegie Hall, I have great news.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:10.020
There's a link in the Doobly-doo there are hundreds of places around the country and the world where you can gather together

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.440
to watch a live stream of the Carnegie Hall event, so go to that link

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:16.240
and find one and then go to one and meet new NerdFighters and et cetera!

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.640
And lastly, Hank, I'm really sorry if something terrible or excellent happened in the last, like, 3 days that I don't know about

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.920
And everyone's like, "why isn't he talking about this in his video??" BECAUSE I'M IN THE PAST!

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.680
Hank, thank you for the 53 wonderful terrible jokes, Don't Forget to be Awesome, I will see you on Saturday.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:34.000
Everyone else will see you on Friday, but I get back on Saturday....I will see you then.

